A||||14||jlruiz67||Great find at FOCOA||||14||
Z||000000||jlruiz67||01-16-2001||11:48 PM||||I'm a member of FOCOA and on the 3rd quarter 2000 mag. I found a great deal that you might like. Here is the full article:<P>"It has come to our attention that we have accumulated lots of Fiero stuff over the years. We have a big warehouse with cars and parts here that we pay lots of money just to store and we have decided to sell off some of the Fieros. It seems a shame to keep the cars when fewer and fewer people come to see them. These cars are for the serious buyers only. Here is what we have if anyone is interested.<P>1.	Pace Car with less than 12 miles on the odometer. We are the 5th owner and the car has never been registered. Excellent car to keep pristine or to make into a show car. If you always wanted an Official Pace Car now you can get one and it’s brand new. Standard trans. Well worth $20K may be last chance to own a new Fiero. Never been registered.<BR>2.	1984 Red w/tan interior Sports Coupe with les than 1.5K miles on the odometer. This car has lots of extras and a really good buy at $6,000.<BR>3.	The only signed 1988 Yellow Formula w/factory T-tops. Very low (1.1K) mileage. 1 of 31 that was built and the first Fiero to ever be signed by workers. Full picture documentation of car being built. First $40,000 takes it. Delivery included. 46 Enterra kit white w/gray interior on 86 Fiero. Lets make a deal.<BR>4.	1988 black/gray interior GT with less than 70K miles. Auto without rear wing. Can supply wing if you are interested in installing. Four now tires. $5,000 OBO.<BR>5.	(2) Pace Car Replicar Kidde go-cart bodies and one Go-Cart frame. We also have the display frame that the assembler cart and body sets on. These retail for over a $700 ea. Are new, cart never driven.<BR>6.	A Fiero trailer that is called ½ Pace. This looks really good behind a Pace car when you go to Fiero Shows. This is a real Pace Car that was cut in half to make a traveling trailer. There is a storage space where the engine was to be. A soda dispenser where the gasoline line used to be. A drop down table in the front. See you would be set up to go either on a trip or camping. All the space you need and that is not in your original Fiero. $1,000 OBO Interested? Give us a call we are willing to negotiate on this item.<P><BR>For those of you, who just read the above listing, do not panic, spread rumors of our demise or think that we have lost our minds. We are simply trying to find homes for some really great Fieros and to cut down on operating cost. We do not have to sell these cars but they are available. They should go to people who will enjoy them, save them for posterity or simply buy a car you could not find elsewhere. They have served their time in the FOCOA museum and need a new/different home."<BR>Please contact:<P>Fiero Owners Club Of America<BR>1598 S. Anaheim Blvd. Unit B<BR>Anaheim, CA. 02805-6230<P>Phone 714-635-0898<BR>Fax 714-917-2161<P>I'm just passing the information.<P><BR><p>[This message has been edited by jlruiz67 (edited 01-17-2001).]||||reg||14
